{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyG8FUydTJnoYAE6wrAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Response to Ticket\n\n**1. Wire `check:pricing-sync` into the pre-commit hook as a BLOCKING check.**\n\nAdd the script to the pre-commit hook configuration and run it at every commit. This catches the coupling break at edit time, before it reaches CI, and the baseline passes cleanly so it won't block unrelated work.\n\n**2. Do NOT delete the `pricing-sync` job from CI; instead, convert it from a blocking required check to a non-blocking advisory job (or retain it as required).**\n\nThe pre-commit hook runs only on developer machines and can be skipped or bypassed; the CI job is the authoritative ship gate that cannot be circumvented. Per the governing doctrine, the earliest layer (pre-commit) catches and surfaces the break fast, but the ship gate retains final authority — delete the CI job only if you are certain all commits will flow through the pre-commit hook with no exceptions (e.g., direct pushes, force pushes, or commits authored outside your hook environment). In practice, keep the CI job required to enforce the invariant at merge time regardless of how code entered the branch."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":595,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":252,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
